{{!-- The route line and its arrowheads, over one regional map. Its context is one `map` object
      from dialogs/journey-map-layer.js `journeyMapLayer`.

      ITS OWN PARTIAL so every surface that draws a route draws the same line: the GM’s pin layer
      (expedition-journey-pins.hbs) and the players’ view of a shared route
      (shared-route-pins.hbs) both include it. --}}
{{!-- The way they go: one bowed leg per stop, joined into a single curve. The viewBox is the
  same 0-100 percentage space the pins are placed in, stretched to the picture by
  preserveAspectRatio="none" — so the curve needs no conversion either, since stretching a
  quadratic leaves a quadratic and leaves it smooth where two of them meet. `vector-effect`
  then keeps the stroke and its dots round and evenly spaced in SCREEN space, which that
  stretch would otherwise smear along one axis. Sits above the map and below the pins, and
  takes no clicks. --}}
{{#if path}}
<svg class="stonetop-journey-path" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path class="stonetop-journey-path-case" d="{{path.d}}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></path>
  <path class="stonetop-journey-path-ink" d="{{path.d}}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></path>
</svg>
{{/if}}

{{!-- Which way they are walking: one head short of every stop the route arrives at, the last of
  them on the destination. Each is its own fixed-size SVG rather than a marker on the polyline
  above: that one is stretched to the picture, which would both squash the head and (with
  orient="auto") aim it off a diagonal. These are sized in pixels and turned by an angle already
  worked out in the box's real proportions, taken from the curve where the head sits rather than
  from the straight line between the stops, so each one lies along the leg it belongs to.

  The TRIANGLE is `path.headD`, not written out here: the Scene painter draws the same head from
  the same points (utils/route-path.js ROUTE_HEAD_POINTS), and a shape spelt out in both places is
  one that gets reshaped in one of them. `../` reaches the map object the `{{#each}}` was opened
  from, which is this partial's own context under both callers. --}}
{{#each path.arrows}}
<svg class="stonetop-journey-arrowhead{{#if waypoint}} stonetop-journey-arrowhead--waypoint{{/if}}"
     viewBox="0 0 10 10" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
     style="left:{{this.left}}%;top:{{this.top}}%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) rotate({{this.angle}}deg)">
  <path d="{{../path.headD}}"></path>
</svg>
{{/each}}
